# The private build pipeline. These two scripts name the client, a named individual and
# the candidate pilot areas. They belong in the private repository that produces this
# one, never here: this repository is the PUBLIC output, hosted on GitHub Pages, and
# tools/build_public_demo.py is the sanitiser whose whole job is to keep those terms out
# of it. They are kept on disk for reference and are never to be committed.
tools/build_demo_data.py
tools/build_public_demo.py

# Merge leftovers. A committed .orig is 90 KB of dead weight with conflict markers
# still in it, and it will be served by Pages and found by every grep.
*.orig
*.rej
*.gitignore


# 1 = more likely to block

# Factor	            Rule
# Bore	                inverted and normalised over the network's own range — the smallest pipe scores 1
# Age	                same, the oldest scores 1
# Gradient	            (1% − grade) / 1%, so at or above self-cleansing it scores 0, flatter scores higher
# Material	            table lookup: VC 1.0, RC 0.7, uPVC 0.3
# Joint	                table lookup: BIT 1.0, SCJ 0.8, PLAST 0.4, RRJ 0.3
# Length	            saturating at 100 m — a 400 m reach isn't four times the problem



Array	    Source field	            Meaning
dia	        NOMINALDIA	                named size, mm → m
idia	    INTERNALDI	                actual bore; carried, unused
mat	        MATERIAL + MATERIALUN	    VC / PVCU / RC, as a code index
year	    CONST_YEAR	                construction year
grade	    GRADE	                    the publisher's own gradient, %
joint	    JOINTTYPE	                RRJ / SCJ / PLAST / BIT



